Well... I was hoping that my first post was going to be YAFAP... and it
looked good for a while, too...

However, Kahlene the Valkyrie has gone on to valhalla the easy way...

It started out looking good. Found an aligned altar on level three with
a sink in the room. Sac'd a little bit, but I don't do much of
sac-fests with low level characters. I find that my hunger rate
typically is faster than the spawn rate...  So, for whatever reason, I
started to quaff from the sink. Got a cursed ring, and then the typical
stupid thing happens: "Water Elemental." Well... I have an altar, so
I'm not going to give this character up without a fight... (Or, atleast
without running around in desperation... So run I do... With the
blasted thing (I thought) at my heels, I run my way straight into a
shop. Dead end. Casting about for anything that can help me, I grab a
lamp, pay up, and start rubbing. Voila, a happy Djinni shows up and
gives me a wish... Normally, at this point in the game, I would be
wishing for a =oSD (hunger being my typical concern) But with an angry
water elemental being on the way, I don't think that would help...
Since all I want to do is survive, I decide that armor is my best bet.
I hear all kinds of cool things about grey dragons, but since I've not
even touched the mines, and I typically find atleast one gnome lucky
enough to have a wand or two, I go for the silver. I ask for blessed
+2, and get blessed +0... But hey, who's complaining? Well... Hit and
run tactics later, the elemental is dead.

I then managed to spend a good amount of time in the mines,
carefully bringing my character up level by level. A coaligned altar in
Minetown brings me Firebrand, Frostbrand, Mjollnir, and Trollbane.
Sokoban was a pain in the neck, including running back and forth
between the mines and Sokoban to retrieve a pick-axe. (I had been
blessed with three scrolls of earth.) Didn't get much interesting in
the way of rewards, but I did manage to find a wand of wishing. I think
I got 4 or 5 wishes out of this. I pretty much squandered them. But I
did end up with a blessed +2 robe. Wasn't worried about the =oSD
anymore, as I was typcially carrying about 6 or seven food rations
around.

Completed Sokoban and was sitting at level 14... So I went on down to
the quest. I smacked fire ants around like the was no tomorrow, and
even fire giants really didn't touch me. I was feeling pretty good.
(Had amulet of breathing on, too, so I survived a few dunks in the ice)
Suddenly, I watch in horror as I am blinded and paragraph after
paragraph of attacks scroll down my screen... Huh?..

Kahlene, killed by a fire giant while helpless

I'm still not sure what hit me.
Oh well... Someone in Hearse can have the pickings.


